1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,620
The 9 times table
with 10 fingers!

2
00:00:04,670 --> 00:00:06,490
Hold up both hands, palms facing you!

3
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:08,640
Starting from the left pinky:
1, 2, 3 … 10

4
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:12,190
For 9 × 3,
fold finger number 3

5
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,160
Fold finger number 3

6
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:15,930
2 fingers left of the fold
→ tens digit 2

7
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:17,700
7 on the right
→ ones digit 7

8
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:19,770
9 × 3 = 27, correct!

9
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:21,740
Your turn! What is 9 × 7?

10
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:27,740
Which finger do you fold?

11
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:29,710
6 on the left, 3 on the right → 63!

12
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:34,880
9 × 4? 9 × 9?

13
00:00:34,930 --> 00:00:37,050
9 is 1 less than 10

14
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:38,680
3 rows of 10 = 30

15
00:00:38,730 --> 00:00:41,050
Take away 3 and you get 9 × 3

16
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,420
2 full rows → tens digit 2
(fingers left of the fold)

17
00:00:43,470 --> 00:00:45,790
The last row has 10 − 3 = 7
(fingers right of the fold)

18
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:49,360
That's why your fingers know the answer

19
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:52,010
Works for 9 × 1 through 9 × 10!

20
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:54,510
NEXT: Times 11 —
split and add!
